[{:db/id 17592186083573 :question/problem "Suppose there are $7$ people who enter a race. Assuming there are no ties, in how many ways can the gold, silver, and bronze medals be awarded?" :question/worked-solution "The number of permutations of $n$ objects taken $r$ at a time is given by the formula\n\n$$\n{}_{n}{P}_{r}=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!}.\n$$\n\nThere are $7$ people, so $n=7.$ We want to select $3$ of those people for gold, silver and bronze, so we have $r=3.$ \n\nTherefore, the number of different ways to award the medals is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{}_{7}{P}_{3} & =\\frac{7!}{(7-3)!} \\\\  & =\\frac{7!}{4!} \\\\  & =\\frac{7\\cdot 6\\cdot 5\\cdot \\cancel{4!}}{\\cancel{4!}} \\\\  & =7\\cdot 6\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =210.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186080333 :answer-field/correct 17592186080335 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186083222 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-9a0bfa46-736f-571e-9fd1-af2e7c4186b1"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-9a0bfa46-736f-571e-9fd1-af2e7c4186b1" :question/id #uuid "9a0bfa46-736f-571e-9fd1-af2e7c4186b1" :question/math-academy-id "q-84984" :question/problem "A soccer coach must choose a defensive lineup for each of the $4$ defensive positions from a roster of $11$ defenders. How many potential starting defensive lineups are there?" :question/worked-solution "The number of permutations of $n$ objects taken $r$ at a time is given by the formula\n\n$$\n{}_{n}{P}_{r}=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!}.\n$$\n\nThere are $11$ defenders, so $n=11.$ We want to select $4$ of those defenders to play in each of the $4$ positions, so we have $r=4.$\n\nTherefore, the number of different starting defensive lineups is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{}_{11}{P}_{4} & =\\frac{11!}{(11-4)!} \\\\  & =\\frac{11!}{7!} \\\\  & =\\frac{11\\cdot 10\\cdot 9\\cdot 8\\cdot \\cancel{7!}}{\\cancel{7!}} \\\\  & =11\\cdot 10\\cdot 9\\cdot 8 \\\\  & =7\\,920.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-69ac052e-a374-5b6c-af86-f7bda6ec7c19"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-69ac052e-a374-5b6c-af86-f7bda6ec7c19" :answer-field/id #uuid "69ac052e-a374-5b6c-af86-f7bda6ec7c19" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-ea315232-2913-5a30-877a-c82272b5ac01" :answer-field/choices ["answer-862c4b09-9172-545f-97c9-7f21e79cd3de" "answer-5456ddc8-8ae6-57cd-97e3-f1eaa26ffc00" "answer-e7a2ab60-18b2-5943-9f8e-856a28f1c403" "answer-ea315232-2913-5a30-877a-c82272b5ac01" "answer-4519364a-a039-5b52-8828-103d442a03a0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-862c4b09-9172-545f-97c9-7f21e79cd3de" :answer/id #uuid "862c4b09-9172-545f-97c9-7f21e79cd3de" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1\\,980" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5456ddc8-8ae6-57cd-97e3-f1eaa26ffc00" :answer/id #uuid "5456ddc8-8ae6-57cd-97e3-f1eaa26ffc00" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\,400" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e7a2ab60-18b2-5943-9f8e-856a28f1c403" :answer/id #uuid "e7a2ab60-18b2-5943-9f8e-856a28f1c403" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "55\\,440" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ea315232-2913-5a30-877a-c82272b5ac01" :answer/id #uuid "ea315232-2913-5a30-877a-c82272b5ac01" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7\\,920" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4519364a-a039-5b52-8828-103d442a03a0" :answer/id #uuid "4519364a-a039-5b52-8828-103d442a03a0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "990" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-f2ef9b69-01fa-553b-9a02-e77367cdec27" :activity/id #uuid "f2ef9b69-01fa-553b-9a02-e77367cdec27" :activity/title "Permutations" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186048254 :activity/course 17592186046658 :activity/steps ["step-fd11f4d8-2ca8-5342-ad46-6e479321